IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Article 12, directories of subscribers.
-- LAYER 1. JUST TRUE = the text says yes, JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words, NOTHING = not covered (NOTES.md,
-- "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- The Article is addressed to Member States ("Member States shall ensure that subscribers are ..."); the functions ask what the
-- subscriber must be given, so that a subscriber, a directory provider or a regulator can read the same answer.

§ `Article 12 -- directories of subscribers`

§§ `Art 12(1) -- information before inclusion`

-- src:116 | Member States shall ensure that subscribers are informed, free of charge and before they are included in the directory, about the purpose(s) of a printed or electronic directory of subscribers available to the public or obtainable through directory enquiry services, in which their personal data can be included and of any further usage possibilities based on search functions embedded in electronic versions of the directory.
@ref Art 12(1) (src:116) row:A12(1)
GIVEN `the directory is a printed or electronic directory of subscribers, available to the public or obtainable through directory enquiry services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber's personal data can be included in the directory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(1) the subscriber must be informed before inclusion in the directory` MEANS
    IF `the directory is a printed or electronic directory of subscribers, available to the public or obtainable through directory enquiry services` AND `the subscriber's personal data can be included in the directory`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for a printed or electronic directory available to the public or obtainable through directory enquiry services, in which the subscriber's personal data can be included
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the subscriber was informed about the purpose or purposes of the directory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directory has search functions embedded in an electronic version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber was informed of the further usage possibilities based on those search functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was given before the subscriber was included in the directory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(1) the subscriber's information before inclusion is as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subscribers are informed, free of charge and before they are included in the directory, about the purpose(s) of a printed or electronic directory"
        IF (NOT `the subscriber was informed about the purpose or purposes of the directory`) OR (NOT `the information was free of charge`) OR (NOT `the information was given before the subscriber was included in the directory`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "of any further usage possibilities based on search functions embedded in electronic versions of the directory"
        IF `the directory has search functions embedded in an electronic version` AND (NOT `the subscriber was informed of the further usage possibilities based on those search functions`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Art 12(2) -- the subscriber decides what is included, and may verify, correct or withdraw`

-- src:117 | Member States shall ensure that subscribers are given the opportunity to determine whether their personal data are included in a public directory, and if so, which, to the extent that such data are relevant for the purpose of the directory as determined by the provider of the directory, and to verify, correct or withdraw such data.
@ref Art 12(2) first sentence (src:117) row:A12(2).s1
GIVEN `the directory is a public directory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(2) first sentence the subscriber must be given the opportunity to determine the inclusion of the personal data and to verify, correct or withdraw it` MEANS
    IF `the directory is a public directory`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about a public directory
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the subscriber was given the opportunity to determine whether their personal data are included` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is relevant for the purpose of the directory as determined by the provider of the directory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber was given the opportunity to determine which of the data are included` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber was given the opportunity to verify the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber was given the opportunity to correct the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber was given the opportunity to withdraw the data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(2) first sentence the subscriber's opportunity is as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subscribers are given the opportunity to determine whether their personal data are included in a public directory"
        IF NOT `the subscriber was given the opportunity to determine whether their personal data are included` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and to verify, correct or withdraw such data"
        IF (NOT `the subscriber was given the opportunity to verify the data`) OR (NOT `the subscriber was given the opportunity to correct the data`) OR (NOT `the subscriber was given the opportunity to withdraw the data`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which, to the extent that such data are relevant for the purpose of the directory as determined by the provider" -- for data that is not relevant the text does not give the choice of which
        IF NOT `the data is relevant for the purpose of the directory as determined by the provider of the directory` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if so, which, to the extent that such data are relevant for the purpose of the directory"
        IF NOT `the subscriber was given the opportunity to determine which of the data are included` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:117 | Not being included in a public subscriber directory, verifying, correcting or withdrawing personal data from it shall be free of charge.
@ref Art 12(2) second sentence (src:117) row:A12(2).s2
GIVEN `not being included in the public subscriber directory was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `verifying personal data was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `correcting personal data was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `withdrawing personal data from the directory was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(2) second sentence the subscriber's non-inclusion, verifying, correcting and withdrawing are free of charge` MEANS
    IF `not being included in the public subscriber directory was free of charge`
       AND `verifying personal data was free of charge`
       AND `correcting personal data was free of charge`
       AND `withdrawing personal data from the directory was free of charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not being included in a public subscriber directory, verifying, correcting or withdrawing personal data from it shall be free of charge"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 12(3) -- additional consent for other purposes`

-- src:118 | Member States may require that for any purpose of a public directory other than the search of contact details of persons on the basis of their name and, where necessary, a minimum of other identifiers, additional consent be asked of the subscribers.
@ref Art 12(3) (src:118) row:A12(3)
GIVEN `the purpose of the public directory is other than the search of contact details of persons on the basis of their name and, where necessary, a minimum of other identifiers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(3) the Member State may require additional consent of the subscribers` MEANS
    IF `the purpose of the public directory is other than the search of contact details of persons on the basis of their name and, where necessary, a minimum of other identifiers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may require") whose gate has failed; the text does not close the gate with "only" (grant and power ruling item 1; FORK F13)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Art 12(4) -- natural persons and other subscribers`

-- src:119 | Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall apply to subscribers who are natural persons.
@ref Art 12(4) first sentence (src:119) row:A12(4).s1
GIVEN `the subscriber is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(4) first sentence paragraphs 1 and 2 apply to the subscriber` MEANS
    IF `the subscriber is a natural person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall apply to subscribers who are natural persons" -- no "only"; for any other subscriber the sentence says nothing about paragraphs 1 and 2 (the second sentence turns to them)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:119 | Member States shall also ensure, in the framework of Community law and applicable national legislation, that the legitimate interests of subscribers other than natural persons with regard to their entry in public directories are sufficiently protected.
@ref Art 12(4) second sentence (src:119) row:A12(4).s2
GIVEN `the subscriber is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(4) second sentence the Member State must ensure that the subscriber's legitimate interests with regard to their entry in public directories are sufficiently protected` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the subscriber is a natural person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about subscribers other than natural persons
    ELSE NOTHING
